When they player kills a monster with rolling boulder trap, it depends
on the player's previous knowledge of the trap if he gets credited or
not.

The comment in the source code states clearly that a player shouldn't
be blamed if he didn't know about the rolling boulder trap:
http://nethackwiki.com/wiki/Source:Ref/ohitmon#line216

But on UnNetHack's public server we just had a failed pacifist who
broke pacifist conduct (which may be tracked in UnNetHack) as he
walked on an *unknown* rolling boulder trap:
http://un.nethack.nu/user/spontiff/dumps/spontiff.1310038833.txt.html

Testing that in Vanilla and UnNetHack showed that the code is wrong.

You get credited for the monster's death if you didn't know about the
trap and you don't get credited if you knew about the trap.

In Vanilla it's a bit difficult to see this but if you enable showexp
you see the experience increase (or not).

The fix should be easy enough. Change !otmp->otrapped in mthrowu.c on
line 218 to otmp->otrapped.

